# AI-LEVERAGE PROFESSIONAL EDGE SPRINT
**Objective:** Take codebase from Tier 2 to Tier 3+ AI-leverage maturity
**Duration:** 3 weeks (15 working days)
**Target:** MCP retrieval, specialized agents, context indexing, knowledge base
**Based on:** AI_LEVERAGE_AUDIT_REPORT.md (March 27, 2026)

---

## SPRINT ARCHITECTURE

### Phase 1: Foundation (Days 1-5) - P0 Critical
**Theme:** MCP Retrieval Server + Core Infrastructure
**Outcome:** Working MCP retrieval with context search capabilities

### Phase 2: Specialization (Days 6-10) - P1 High
**Theme:** Specialized Agents + Knowledge Base
**Outcome:** 3 specialist agents + 5 subsystem documentation files

### Phase 3: Optimization (Days 11-15) - P2 Medium
**Theme:** Orchestration + Empty Workflows + Settings Enhancement
**Outcome:** Automated routing, complete workflow coverage, enhanced automation

---

## PHASE 1: FOUNDATION (Days 1-5)

### [P0-1] SCOPE CONTRACT: Extend MCP Server with Retrieval Tools
**Complexity:** 8 (difficult - requires protocol understanding + implementation)
**Estimated Time:** 6-8 hours
**Files to Modify:** `.cursor/mcp-server.js` (ALLOWED WRITE)
**Read-Only Context:** `.windsurf/workflows/`, `_contexts/`, `.cursor/`

#### IN SCOPE
- Extend existing `SangLogiumMCPServer` class in `.cursor/mcp-server.js`
- Add 4 retrieval tools: `searchContext`, `getSubsystemDocs`, `suggestAgent`, `listSubsystems`
- Implement JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol compliance for new tools
- Add error handling and response formatting per MCP spec
- Support both stdio transport (current) and future HTTP transport

#### OUT OF SCOPE
- Do NOT create a new server file - extend existing only
- Do NOT change existing resources (`workflow://instructions`, `workflow://project-context`)
- Do NOT implement semantic/vector search yet (keyword only for this scope)
- Do NOT add authentication or authorization layers

#### FORBIDDEN SCOPE
- No changes to Windsurf/Cascade configuration files yet
- No new agent specifications yet
- No subsystem documentation yet

#### ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS
- Keep extending existing class pattern vs creating new classes
- Use async/await for all tool implementations (future-proofing)
- Keyword search only - vector search is Phase 3 optimization
- Return file paths with relevance scores (0.0-1.0) for consistency

#### DEFINITIONS OF DONE (Complete in order)

- [ ] **DoD 1.1:** Read and understand current `mcp-server.js` structure
  - Read file: `.cursor/mcp-server.js` (exists, 194 lines)
  - Identify: `handleRequest` method pattern, response format, error handling
  - Verify: Server uses stdio transport, JSON-RPC 2.0

- [ ] **DoD 1.2:** Implement `searchContext(query: string)` tool
  - Add to `handleRequest` switch statement: case `"tools/call"` with method `searchContext`
  - Search directories: `_contexts/`, `.windsurf/`, `_project/COMMANDS/`
  - Return format: `{ results: [{ file: string, relevance: number, snippet: string }] }`
  - Relevance scoring: exact match = 1.0, partial = 0.5, directory match = 0.3
  - Max 10 results per query

- [ ] **DoD 1.3:** Implement `getSubsystemDocs(subsystem: string)` tool
  - Map subsystem names to documentation files
  - Support: "vfs", "sanity", "checkout", "drawers", "images" (files may not exist yet)
  - Return: Full file contents or "not found" error
  - Handle case-insensitive subsystem names

- [ ] **DoD 1.4:** Implement `suggestAgent(intent: string)` tool
  - Map intents to workflow files
  - "debug" -> `debug.md`, "implement" -> `implement.md`, "test" -> `test.md`
  - "commit" -> `commit.md`, "sprint" -> `sprint.md`
  - Return: `{ workflow: string, description: string, path: string }`

- [ ] **DoD 1.5:** Implement `listSubsystems()` tool
  - Return array of available subsystem names
  - Based on files found in `_contexts/subsystems/` (directory may not exist yet)
  - Return: `{ subsystems: ["vfs", "sanity", "checkout", ...] }`

- [ ] **DoD 1.6:** Add tools listing capability
  - Extend `tools/list` case in `handleRequest`
  - List all 4 new tools with descriptions and parameter schemas
  - Follow MCP spec for tool definitions

- [ ] **DoD 1.7:** Verification - Test MCP server locally
  - Command: `node .cursor/mcp-server.js` (should start without errors)
  - Test: Send JSON-RPC request via stdin for each new tool
  - Test format: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"searchContext","arguments":{"query":"vfs"}}}`
  - All 4 tools must respond with valid JSON-RPC responses

#### VERIFICATION COMMANDS (Run in sequence)

```powershell
# V1.1 - Type check
npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck .cursor/mcp-server.js

# V1.2 - Lint check
npm run lint .cursor/mcp-server.js

# V1.3 - Manual test - start server and send test request
$testRequest = '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}'
$testRequest | node .cursor/mcp-server.js

# V1.4 - Verify response contains all 4 new tools
# Expected: searchContext, getSubsystemDocs, suggestAgent, listSubsystems
```

