### [P0-2] SCOPE CONTRACT: Create Context Indexing System
**Complexity:** 5 (medium - straightforward file operations)
**Estimated Time:** 3-4 hours
**Files to Create:** `scripts/build-context-index.mjs` (NEW FILE)
**Files to Create:** `data/context-index.json` (GENERATED)
**Read-Only Context:** `_contexts/`, `.windsurf/workflows/`, `_project/`

#### IN SCOPE
- Create Node.js script to index context files by keywords
- Scan directories: `_contexts/`, `.windsurf/workflows/`, `.windsurf/memories/`, `_project/COMMANDS/`
- Generate JSON index mapping keywords to file paths
- Save output to `data/context-index.json`
- Include file metadata: size, lastModified, keywords extracted from filename/content

#### OUT OF SCOPE
- Do NOT implement vector embeddings (Phase 3 only if needed)
- Do NOT create web interface for search
- Do NOT implement real-time file watching
- Do NOT integrate with MCP server yet (Phase 1.3)

#### FORBIDDEN SCOPE
- No changes to existing context file contents
- No deletions of existing files

#### ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS
- Keyword extraction: filename + first 500 chars of content
- Weighting: filename match = 1.0, content match = 0.5
- Index structure: flat object with keyword keys, array of file entries
- Regenerate index manually (no auto-watch) - simpler, more predictable

#### DEFINITIONS OF DONE (Complete in order)

- [ ] **DoD 2.1:** Create `scripts/build-context-index.mjs`
  - File must be executable: `node scripts/build-context-index.mjs`
  - Use ES modules (import syntax consistent with other scripts)
  - Import: `fs`, `path`, `glob` (or use native fs.readdir with recursion)

- [ ] **DoD 2.2:** Implement directory scanning
  - Scan: `_contexts/` (recursive), `.windsurf/workflows/`, `.windsurf/memories/`, `_project/COMMANDS/`
  - File types: `*.md`, `*.json`, `*.ts` (only if in context directories)
  - Exclude: `node_modules`, `.git`, `dist`, `build`

- [ ] **DoD 2.3:** Implement keyword extraction
  - Extract from filename (lowercase, split on -, _, .)
  - Extract from first 500 characters of file content
  - Extract from markdown headers (## Header -> "header" keyword)
  - Normalize: lowercase, remove punctuation

- [ ] **DoD 2.4:** Generate index structure
  - Format: `{ "keywords": { "vfs": [{"file": "...", "relevance": 0.9}], "sanity": [...] }, "files": { "path/to/file.md": { "keywords": [...], "size": 1234 } } }`
  - Sort keywords alphabetically for consistency
  - Sort file entries by relevance descending

- [ ] **DoD 2.5:** Write index to disk
  - Output: `data/context-index.json`
  - Pretty print with 2-space indentation
  - Include timestamp: `_generatedAt: "2026-03-27T..."`

- [ ] **DoD 2.6:** Verification - Build and validate index
  - Run: `node scripts/build-context-index.mjs`
  - Verify: `data/context-index.json` exists and is valid JSON
  - Verify: Contains at least 10 keywords
  - Verify: Keywords "vfs", "sanity", "checkout" exist (if corresponding files exist)

#### VERIFICATION COMMANDS (Run in sequence)

```powershell
# V2.1 - Build index
node scripts/build-context-index.mjs

# V2.2 - Validate JSON output
Get-Content data/context-index.json | ConvertFrom-Json | Out-Null
Write-Host "Valid JSON ✓"

# V2.3 - Check keyword coverage
$index = Get-Content data/context-index.json | ConvertFrom-Json
Write-Host "Total keywords: $($index.keywords.PSObject.Properties.Count)"
Write-Host "Keywords: $($index.keywords.PSObject.Properties.Name -join ', ')"

# V2.4 - Verify index file size reasonable (should be < 500KB)
$fileInfo = Get-Item data/context-index.json
Write-Host "Index size: $($fileInfo.Length) bytes"
```

