### [P0-3] SCOPE CONTRACT: Integrate MCP Server with Context Index
**Complexity:** 5 (medium - integration work)
**Estimated Time:** 2-3 hours
**Files to Modify:** `.cursor/mcp-server.js` (ALLOWED WRITE)
**Read-Only Context:** `data/context-index.json` (generated in P0-2)

#### IN SCOPE
- Update `searchContext` tool to use `data/context-index.json`
- Load index on server startup and cache in memory
- Add relevance scoring based on index data
- Implement basic query parsing (split on spaces, AND logic)

#### OUT OF SCOPE
- Do NOT implement real-time index updates
- Do NOT implement complex query syntax (OR, NOT, wildcards)
- Do NOT implement fuzzy matching

#### FORBIDDEN SCOPE
- No changes to index generation script
- No changes to directory structure

#### ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS
- Load index once at startup (performance)
- Manual restart required after index rebuild (simplicity)
- AND logic for multi-word queries (all terms must match)
- Relevance = average of term relevances

#### DEFINITIONS OF DONE (Complete in order)

- [ ] **DoD 3.1:** Load index in MCP server constructor
  - Read: `data/context-index.json`
  - Cache in: `this.contextIndex`
  - Handle: File not found error gracefully (empty index)

- [ ] **DoD 3.2:** Update `searchContext` to use index
  - Parse query: split on whitespace, lowercase
  - For each keyword, look up in `this.contextIndex.keywords`
  - Implement AND logic: file must match ALL query terms
  - Calculate relevance: average of individual term relevances
  - Sort results by relevance descending
  - Return top 10 results

- [ ] **DoD 3.3:** Add file content preview
  - For each result, read first 200 characters of file
  - Truncate at word boundary
  - Return in `snippet` field

- [ ] **DoD 3.4:** Verification - End-to-end test
  - Ensure index exists: `data/context-index.json`
  - Start server: `node .cursor/mcp-server.js`
  - Send test request: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"searchContext","arguments":{"query":"implement workflow"}}}`
  - Verify: Returns results with files containing "implement" and "workflow"

#### VERIFICATION COMMANDS (Run in sequence)

```powershell
# V3.1 - Ensure index exists
if (-not (Test-Path data/context-index.json)) {
    node scripts/build-context-index.mjs
}

# V3.2 - Type check
npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck .cursor/mcp-server.js

# V3.3 - Lint check
npm run lint .cursor/mcp-server.js

# V3.4 - Manual integration test
# In one terminal: node .cursor/mcp-server.js
# In another terminal, send test request via stdin
$test = '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"searchContext","arguments":{"query":"debug workflow"}}}'
Write-Host "Test with: $test"
```

